  "chunks": [
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Intelligent Systems Engineering (هندسة الأنظمة الذكية) — B.Sc. study plan 2025/2026, Faculty of Engineering & Design, Middle East University.\nThe degree requires 162 credit hours in total:\n- University requirements: 18 credit hours (compulsory)\n- University electives: 6 credit hours\n- Faculty requirements: 24 credit hours (group A: 6, group C: 18 — mathematics, physics, chemistry)\n- Area of study (major) requirements: 83 credit hours\n- Ancillary (supporting) courses: 22 credit hours\n- Area of study (major) electives: 9 credit hours\nRemedial courses (Arabic, English, computer skills) are taken only when required and are not counted in the 162 hours.\nThe plan includes a two-part graduation project (Graduation Project I after 120 completed credit hours, then Graduation Project II) and external Field Training (after 110 completed credit hours)."
    },
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Intelligent Systems Engineering study plan 2025/2026 — approvals and signatories.\nFaculty Council decision 03/06-2025/2026, adopted 06/11/2025. Deans' Council decision 07/15-2025/2026, adopted 30/12/2025.\nHead of Department: Dr. Mohammad Klaib. Dean of the Faculty: Prof. Ayman Abdel Salam Awad. Director of Admissions and Registration: Mrs. Nadia Al-Bakri."
    },
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Intelligent Systems Engineering — robotics, AI and hardware courses in the 2025/2026 study plan:\nRobot Programming (برمجة الروبوت, 1924704), Human Robot Interaction (elective, 1925609), Embedded Systems (1923803), Sensors and Actuators with lab (1924806/1924807), Internet of Things (1924805), Control Systems with lab (1915301/1915302), Micro-Processors (1923802), Introduction to Artificial Intelligence (1922601), Machine Learning (1923603), Deep Learning (1924606), Fuzzy and Neural Networks (1923604), Image Processing & Computer Vision (1924605), Data Science (1922602), Digital Signal Processing (1923402) and Object Oriented Python Programming (1922701)."
    }
  ],
